{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LAotkE7PqiNi4baLkGbrK8","type":"tool_result","content":"| `.bind(signal, element, options?)` | `void` | Bind a signal to a DOM element property, auto-cleaned on teardown. |\n| `.onCleanup(fn)` | `void` | Register custom teardown, run a microtask after disconnect. |\n| `.consume(token)` | `T \\| undefined` | Read an optional context value published by an ancestor. See [`withContexts`](#withcontexts). |\n\nSee [Typed Events](#typed-events) for more about `.on` and `.emit`.\n\n##### `ctx.bind`\n\nThe `.bind` method treats the signal as the source of truth. The element\nproperty is set from the signal.\nWith no `options`, the control's element property and write-back event are\nauto-detected from its type:\n\n```ts\n{\n    bind<T> (\n        source:Signal<T>,\n        control:Element,\n        opts?:BindOptions\n    )\n}\n```\n\n| Control | `prop` | write-back `event` |\n|---------|--------|---------------------|\n| `<input type=\"checkbox\">` | `checked` | `change` |\n| `<input type=\"number\">` / `type=\"range\"` | `valueAsNumber` | `input` |\n| Other `<input>` types / `<textarea>` | `value` | `input` |\n| Anything else, e.g. `<select>` | `value` | `change` |\n\nPassing `options` overrides the auto-detected `prop`, and replaces the\nwrite-back `event` -- omit `options.event` for a one-way binding. A read-only\ngetter (`() => T`) is also accepted as the `signal` argument, for binding a\nderived value one-way (pass it with `options` and omit `event`).\n\n```ts\n// two-way, auto-detected (checkbox -> `checked` / `change`)\nctx.bind(checked, ctx.refs.toggle)\n\n// one-way: push a derived value into a read-only display\nctx.bind(() => `${count()} items`, ctx.refs.label, { prop: 'textContent' })\n```\n\n---\n\n\n## Missing refs\n\nAny calls to `r.one` in `.withRefs` will throw if there is not a matching\nchild element.\n\nREADME.md:26:<!-- toc -->\nREADME.md:96:<!-- tocstop -->\npackage.json:93:    \"toc\": \"markdown-toc --maxdepth 5 -i README.md\",\npackage.json:94:    \"toc:hydration\": \"markdown-toc --maxdepth 3 -i example-hydration/README.md\",\npackage.json:96:    \"version\": \"npm run toc && npm run toc:hydration && auto-changelog -p --template keepachangelog --breaking-pattern 'BREAKING CHANGE:' && npm run inject-size && git add CHANGELOG.md README.md\",\npackage.json:136:    \"markdown-toc\": \"^1.2.0\",","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2610be84-750a-4596-acbd-ed9ce3c7ac4d","uuid":"4f9ffecd-5390-43b3-a908-07d0df155465","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:30:03.471Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"| `.bind(signal, element, options?)` | `void` | Bind a signal to a DOM element property, auto-cleaned on teardown. |\n| `.onCleanup(fn)` | `void` | Register custom teardown, run a microtask after disconnect. |\n| `.consume(token)` | `T \\| undefined` | Read an optional context value published by an ancestor. See [`withContexts`](#withcontexts). |\n\nSee [Typed Events](#typed-events) for more about `.on` and `.emit`.\n\n##### `ctx.bind`\n\nThe `.bind` method treats the signal as the source of truth. The element\nproperty is set from the signal.\nWith no `options`, the control's element property and write-back event are\nauto-detected from its type:\n\n```ts\n{\n    bind<T> (\n        source:Signal<T>,\n        control:Element,\n        opts?:BindOptions\n    )\n}\n```\n\n| Control | `prop` | write-back `event` |\n|---------|--------|---------------------|\n| `<input type=\"checkbox\">` | `checked` | `change` |\n| `<input type=\"number\">` / `type=\"range\"` | `valueAsNumber` | `input` |\n| Other `<input>` types / `<textarea>` | `value` | `input` |\n| Anything else, e.g. `<select>` | `value` | `change` |\n\nPassing `options` overrides the auto-detected `prop`, and replaces the\nwrite-back `event` -- omit `options.event` for a one-way binding. A read-only\ngetter (`() => T`) is also accepted as the `signal` argument, for binding a\nderived value one-way (pass it with `options` and omit `event`).\n\n```ts\n// two-way, auto-detected (checkbox -> `checked` / `change`)\nctx.bind(checked, ctx.refs.toggle)\n\n// one-way: push a derived value into a read-only display\nctx.bind(() => `${count()} items`, ctx.refs.label, { prop: 'textContent' })\n```\n\n---\n\n\n## Missing refs\n\nAny calls to `r.one` in `.withRefs` will throw if there is not a matching\nchild element.\n\nREADME.md:26:<!-- toc -->\nREADME.md:96:<!-- tocstop -->\npackage.json:93:    \"toc\": \"markdown-toc --maxdepth 5 -i README.md\",\npackage.json:94:    \"toc:hydration\": \"markdown-toc --maxdepth 3 -i example-hydration/README.md\",\npackage.json:96:    \"version\": \"npm run toc && npm run toc:hydration && auto-changelog -p --template keepachangelog --breaking-pattern 'BREAKING CHANGE:' && npm run inject-size && git add CHANGELOG.md README.md\",\npackage.json:136:    \"markdown-toc\": \"^1.2.0\",","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LAotkE7PqiNi4baLkGbrK8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
