{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3PpkSAAjdjJqvbzA2Wi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TBGnAawLyjpfCBNZCRmPUt","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"only (mapped types cannot split read and write types).\n\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"only (mapped types cannot split read and write types). To bind a\nsignal with its type checked, use the exported `bindProp(host, name,\nsource)` (in `factory.ts`) rather than a cast. Its prop key is\n`Exclude<keyof H, keyof HTMLElement>`, so its `@ts-expect-error` cases\nin `test/types.ts` import it from `'microtags'` and need a rebuilt\n`dist/`. Do not confuse it with `ctx.bind` (DOM property binding).\nSmall core exports minify shorter as `export const f = () => {}` than\nas `function f () {}`.\n\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old)==1\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# Ticket 09: typed bind helper\n\n## Done\n1. `bindProp(host, name, source)` exported from core (src/factory.ts,\n   re-exported in src/index.ts). Named `bindProp`, not `bind`, because\n   `ctx.bind` already exists with a different meaning (DOM property).\n   Types: `H extends HTMLElement`, `K extends Exclude<keyof H, keyof\n   HTMLElement>`, `source:() => H[K]` so both signals and alien-signals\n   computeds are accepted. Runtime is `host[name] = source`.\n   Browser test: \"bindProp: the host prop reads and tracks the signal\".\n2. test/types.ts: matching signal and computed compile; mismatched\n   types and a non-prop key (`id`) are `@ts-expect-error`. I checked\n   that the expect-errors depend on the real signature by loosening\n   dist/factory.d.ts temporarily (they turned into \"unused directive\").\n3. Counter uses `bindProp(ctx.refs.current, 'label', label)`. The\n   existing \"example Counter\" browser test (count(40) -> badge text 40)\n   covers the nested badge following the computed; a