{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3PuJregLw9rT5yCQpGQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, `npm run test:hydration` and `npm run size` pass\n\nTicket 09 is done in four commits. Core now exports `bindProp(host, name, source)`, and Counter uses it in place of the `as unknown as string` cast.\n\nAt runtime it just does `host[name] = source`, the same as assigning the signal to the prop accessor. The type allows only the host's declared props, not ordinary `HTMLElement` properties like `id`. The source's value type must match the prop's type. It takes a writable signal or an alien-signals `computed`.\n\n**Naming:** I called it `bindProp` rather than `bind` because setup already has `ctx.bind`, which binds a signal to a DOM property. Two `bind`s that do different things would be confusing.\n\n**Checks:**\n1. A browser test binds a computed with `bindProp` and confirms that the host prop reads it, follows later changes, and that the component's setup effect tracks it.\n2. Type tests in `test/types.ts` import `bindProp` from `'microtags'`. A matching signal and computed compile. A wrong value type, in either direction, and a non-prop key are `@ts-expect-error`. I loosened the built signature for a moment to confirm those three lines really depend on it, then restored it.\n3. The existing `example Counter` browser test already checks that the nested Badge's text follows the count. It still passes, and I switched its own cast to `bindProp`. The Playwright e2e suite also passes (12 tests).\n4. Lint, typecheck, `npm test` (416), `npm run test:ssr`, `npm run test:hydration` (114 + 17) and `npm run size` all pass.\n\n**Size:** written as a `function`, the helper put core 4 B over its 4.3 kB limit. As an arrow function core measures 4.28 kB, so `.size-limit.js` is unchanged.\n\n**Docs:**\n- The README has a new `bindProp` API section. Regenerating its table of contents also removed some old Hydration entries whose headings no longer exist.\n- The **Prop** entry in CONTEXT.md mentions `bindProp`, and so does the Counter note in the example README.\n- The `MicrotagHost` doc comment no longer suggests a cast.\n- AGENTS.md has a short note on `bindProp`, how to keep its type tests working, and the arrow-function size trick.\n\nMy notes for this attempt are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":304,"cache_read_input_tokens":85990,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":304},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2610be84-750a-4596-acbd-ed9ce3c7ac4d","uuid":"3a398c55-9dae-42cb-aac0-16d7f311c578","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:31:32.230Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3PuJa3g16CfGh1TcVvf"}
